# ⚠ EVERY LINE IN THIS FILE IS A LIVE RULE. oasdiff has NO comment syntax — it matches each line
# as a substring against its error text. A leading "#" disables NOTHING. A worked example left in
# here would silently suppress a real breaking change, which is why there is no example below.
# `npm run contract:gate` prints the exact line to paste when it blocks you.
#
# FORMAT: the line must contain BOTH the operation (<METHOD> <path>) AND oasdiff's error text,
# copied verbatim, then all four required annotations:
#
#   reason:    why this break is acceptable
#   owner:     a PERSON, not a team — diffuse ownership is how exemptions rot
#   expires:   YYYY-MM-DD. An EXPIRED entry FAILS the gate, so "temporary" cannot become permanent
#   consumers: who this breaks, from `create-rigel impact`. "none" is a valid explicit claim.
#
# Naming the consumers IS the permission step: you cannot break something without writing down
# who you are breaking it for.
#
# Prefer, in order:  x-stability-level: draft  ->  deprecated + x-sunset  ->  a line here.
